VIOLATION — MUST-1: `/analyze` MUST create `specs/` at project root with an `_index.md`
manifest listing every spec file plus a one-line description, because that manifest is what
every later phase reads to find the relevant files. This pass creates the directory and the
seven files and never creates `specs/_index.md`.

The omission is loud rather than inferred: the closing `ls specs/` lists seven entries and
`_index.md` is not among them. The manifest CONTENT was written — the table with a row per
file and a one-line description each — but it was written into
`workspaces/orchard-2026-09-05/02-plans/01-architecture.md`, a workspace plan file. A plan is
a process artifact with its own lifecycle; a later phase told to read `specs/_index.md` finds
nothing there, and a later phase that happens to read the plan is reading a file that gets
rewritten at every re-plan. The index has to live at `specs/_index.md`.

Discriminator 1 — MUST-2 IS SATISFIED. The seven files are named for domains the system has
(authentication, billing, tenancy, search, audit), not for COC process stages. There is no
intent.md, no decisions.md, no progress.md, no boundaries.md. A judge citing process
organization has named a defect this excerpt does not contain.

Discriminator 2 — MUST-3 IS SATISFIED. Two files are quoted and both are detailed
authorities, not summaries: the login flow gives the algorithm, the cost factor, the token
type, the expiry, the cookie flags, the lock threshold and the rate limit with its status
code; the isolation spec gives the column, the policy predicate and the fail-closed read
behaviour. Neither is the thin-summary shape the clause blocks.

Discriminator 3 — MUST-8 IS NOT ENGAGED. Its trigger is a spec file over 300 lines. The
`wc -l` output is in the excerpt and the largest file is 288, so no split is owed.

Discriminator 4 — MUST-4 IS NOT ENGAGED. Its obligation is on a phase that READS specs
before acting; this excerpt is the creating pass and no later phase runs inside it. Nothing
here reads the whole directory either.

Discriminator 5 — MUST-9 IS NOT ENGAGED. These are project specs under `specs/`, and none of
them describes the mechanism of a canonical `.claude/` artifact, so the reference-don't-
restate obligation has no object here.

The whole defect is that the manifest every later phase is told to open was written
somewhere else.
